From: Emerson Busson <emersonbusson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:34:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH v2 4/6] test(hv): correct VMBus fallback order vector

Use the order that matches the remaining page count in the fallback
helper test.

Signed-off-by: Emerson Busson <emersonbusson@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/hv/channel.c b/drivers/hv/channel.c
index 091288f8c00c8426480c08a1c91900c2e94afcb0..c47a923306f298291b169c5827c777082ba1b162 100644
--- a/drivers/hv/channel.c
+++ b/drivers/hv/channel.c
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ static void vmbus_ring_fallback_order_zero_test(struct kunit *test)
 {
 	unsigned int order;
 
-	order = vmbus_buffer_order(128, MAX_PAGE_ORDER);
+	order = vmbus_buffer_order(1UL << MAX_PAGE_ORDER, MAX_PAGE_ORDER);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, order, (unsigned int)MAX_PAGE_ORDER);
 	while (order)
 		KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, vmbus_buffer_lower_order(&order));
-- 
